course: dictionary
lesson: 6271
title: Mongol: a people and an empire
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mongol is a word with two jobs. It can name people, like «the Mongols», or describe something, like «Mongol horsemen». When it names people, it is a noun. When it describes something, it is an adjective. Always write it with a capital M.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is which. «Temujin united the Mongol tribes» uses Mongol to describe the tribes, so it is an adjective. «The Mongol Empire» is a huge empire in history, not the people themselves.
explain: Look at the words near Mongol to find its meaning. «After the conquests the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely across Asia.» Lands tells you Mongol means the place and the people who ruled it. Safe travel tells you the empire was big and well run.
fact: Mongol is written with a capital M.
fact: The Mongols are the people of Mongolia and nearby lands in Central and East Asia.
fact: Traditionally, Mongol herders moved with their animals and lived in round felt tents called gers or yurts.
fact: «Mongol» can also describe the Mongol Empire, the largest joined land empire in history, stretching from China to Eastern Europe.
fact: In 1206 Temujin was named Genghis Khan, meaning universal ruler.
exercise: «Temujin united the Mongol tribes and in 1206 was named Genghis Khan.» What kind of word is Mongol here? | A verb, an action word | A noun, the name of a person | *An adjective, describing the tribes | A number
exercise: «In December 1240 the Mongol army under Batu took Kyiv.» What is Mongol describing in this sentence? | Kyiv | *The army | The winter month | Batu himself
exercise: Mongol herders moved with their animals and lived in round felt tents. What were these tents called? | *Gers or yurts | Igloos | Wigwams | Castles
test: «The Mongol Empire was the largest joined land empire in history.» What does Mongol Empire mean? | A small village by a river | A type of horse only | *The huge empire built by Genghis Khan and his family | A modern school subject
test: Which sentence about Mongolia today is true? | It is in Africa | It has no grasslands | It is an island in the Pacific | *It is a country between Russia and China
exam: «After the conquests the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely.» What did the Mongol peace allow? | *Traders to travel safely across Asia | Fight the Ming dynasty | Stop all trade | Build huge castles
